out 15 minutes" and gives the exact start time separately: asserting a precision the delivery mechanism does not have trains students to distrust the timing. Vercel's three cron slots are spent and are hourly or daily, so they could not serve this even if one were free. The idempotency key is scoped to (kind, class, recipient) and NOT to enqueue time, so an instructor editing a class three times sends one email — with the deliberate consequence, written down, that a genuine reschedule does not re-notify, and the fix when somebody wants it is to add the start timestamp to the key for the `scheduled` kind exactly as gradedNotificationKey includes graded_at. formatClassTime NAMES THE TIME ZONE in every string, because a cohort spread across zones reading "18:00" has no way to know whose and the failure is a student joining an hour late; it uses explicit Intl components rather than dateStyle/timeStyle, which THROW "Invalid option" when combined with timeZoneName — found by running it, not by typechecking. | feature/lms-complete-enhancement
