2026-08-07T00:00:00Z | SUBMIT-SYNC-004 | src/app/(staff)/instructor/grading/page.tsx | MODIFY | Placed the sync button in the grading-queue header (header made flex row/column responsive). This is the surface where the gap is felt: Form responses arrive on a scheduled sweep, so a submission made minutes ago is not in the queue yet and the instructor had no way to force a read. No data flow changed — the page's queries are untouched. | feature/manual-submission-sync

2026-08-07T00:00:00Z | SUBMIT-SYNC-005 | src/app/(app)/assignments/ingest-status/page.tsx | MODIFY | Same button on the operator surface, which previously instructed the reader to POST to an API by hand. Header prose corrected: it claimed hourly sweeps while vercel.json schedules ingestion daily ("0 0 * * *"), so it now says "on a schedule" rather than restating a cadence that was wrong. | feature/manual-submission-sync

2026-08-07T00:00:00Z | SUBMIT-SYNC-006 | tests/e2e/submissions/submissions.spec.ts | MODIFY | Three e2e specs: a student sees the button on neither surface (both redirect), an instructor's press on the grading queue records a run whose `triggeredBy` is "manual" on the status API (proving the press reached the write path rather than only rendering a toast), and an admin can press it on the ingest-status page. Suite timeout raised to 180 000 ms for this block only — the sweep fetches one CSV per assignment sequentially at up to 15 000 ms each and measured ~15 s end to end, over the 30 000 ms default once page compilation is included. VERIFIED: 3 passed against a real dev server and database. | feature/manual-submission-sync
